#. Tag: title
#: footendnotes.docbook:11
#, no-c-format
msgid "Footnotes and Endnotes"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: primary
#: footendnotes.docbook:12 footendnotes.docbook:25 footendnotes.docbook:63
#: footendnotes.docbook:79 footendnotes.docbook:87
#, no-c-format
msgid "footnotes"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: secondary
#: footendnotes.docbook:12 footendnotes.docbook:13
#, no-c-format
msgid "introduction"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: primary
#: footendnotes.docbook:13 footendnotes.docbook:26 footendnotes.docbook:64
#: footendnotes.docbook:80 footendnotes.docbook:166
#, no-c-format
msgid "endnotes"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: footendnotes.docbook:15
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kword; has a complete set of tools to create and manage footnotes and "
"endnotes. When you assign a footnote, &kword; automatically places the "
"footnote at the bottom of the correct page. When you assign an endnote, the "
"notation is located in a numbered list at the end of your text. If the "
"footnote or endnote reference point is moved to a new page, the footnote "
"automatically follows and is renumbered as needed (if the user desires)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: footendnotes.docbook:19
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kword; also has the ability to separately manage endnotes and footnotes in "
"the same document."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: footendnotes.docbook:20
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You have the option of having &kword; control the numbering of your "
"footnotes. Alternatively, you can manually specify each footnote."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: footendnotes.docbook:21
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"There are multiple automatic numbering schemes and your footnotes can be "
"separated from the text with a dividing line."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: footendnotes.docbook:24
#, no-c-format
msgid "Add a new footnote or endnote"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: secondary
#: footendnotes.docbook:25 footendnotes.docbook:26
#, no-c-format
msgid "creating"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: footendnotes.docbook:28
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To add a new footnote or endnote, place your cursor at the end of the text "
"you want to reference. Then select <menuchoice><guimenu>Insert</"
"guimenu><guimenuitem>Footnote/Endnote...</guimenuitem></menuchoice> from the "
"menubar. This will bring up a dialog box."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: footendnotes.docbook:40
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you want &kword; to automatically number your footnotes or endnotes for "
"you, make sure that <guilabel>Automatic</guilabel> is selected. If you want "
"to manually enter all footnotes in, then select <guilabel>Manual</guilabel> "
"and enter the footnote or endnote entry in the text box to the right."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: footendnotes.docbook:43
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If at all possible, try to allow &kword; to automatically number the "
"footnotes and endnotes for you. If &kword; controls the numbering, and you "
"insert, delete or move footnotes, &kword; will automatically renumber or "
"reorder the footnotes for you."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: footendnotes.docbook:46
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Then select either <guilabel>Footnote</guilabel> or <guilabel>Endnote</"
"guilabel>. Footnotes will appear at the bottom of the page where the "
"notation occurs. Endnotes will appear as an ordered list at the end of your "
"document."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: footendnotes.docbook:49
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Click <guibutton>Configure</guibutton> to <link linkend=\"fn-config\">change "
"the look</link> of your footnotes or endnotes."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: footendnotes.docbook:50
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Click <guibutton>Cancel</guibutton> to return to your document without "
"inserting a footnote or endnote."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: footendnotes.docbook:52
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Click <guibutton>OK</guibutton> to insert the footnote or endnote. &kword; "
"will create the footnote or endnote entry, and place the cursor at the "
"beginning of the entry for you to enter the desired reference information. "
"Type your reference information in the space provided."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: footendnotes.docbook:56
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When you have finished entering your footnote or endnote reference "
"information, simply move your cursor over the footnote or endnote number. "
"Click with the &RMB;. A popup menu will appear. Select <guilabel>Go to "
"Footnote</guilabel> and &kword; will move the cursor back to the text where "
"the reference was made."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: footendnotes.docbook:62
#, no-c-format
msgid "Change reference of footnote"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: secondary
#: footendnotes.docbook:63 footendnotes.docbook:64
#, no-c-format
msgid "editing"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: footendnotes.docbook:66
#, no-c-format
msgid "There are two ways to change reference information for a footnote:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: footendnotes.docbook:68
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Place the mouse pointer over the footnote you want to change, and click once "
"with the &RMB;. A popup menu will appear. Select <guimenuitem>Edit Footnote</"
"guimenuitem>. &kword; will immediately move your cursor to the appropriate "
"footnote reference."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: footendnotes.docbook:71
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Simply move to the bottom of the page (if it is a footnote) or the end of "
"the document (if it is an endnote). Locate the footnote or endnote "
"reference, and click once with the &LMB;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: footendnotes.docbook:73
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can jump to the end of the document by typing <keycombo action=\"simul"
"\">&Ctrl;<keycap>End</keycap></keycombo>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: footendnotes.docbook:78
#, no-c-format
msgid "Delete a footnote or endnote"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: secondary
#: footendnotes.docbook:79 footendnotes.docbook:80
#, no-c-format
msgid "deleting"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: footendnotes.docbook:82
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To delete a footnote, simply delete the footnote or endnote number. &kword; "
"will remove the reference information and resize the footnote frame."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: footendnotes.docbook:86
#, no-c-format
msgid "Change the look of footnotes"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: secondary
#: footendnotes.docbook:87 footendnotes.docbook:166
#, no-c-format
msgid "change appearance"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: footendnotes.docbook:89
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To configure the appearance of footnotes, select <menuchoice> "
"<guimenu>Format</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Footnote...</guimenuitem></"
"menuchoice> from the menubar. A dialog will appear."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: footendnotes.docbook:99 footendnotes.docbook:186
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"There are 5 predefined numbering methods for footnotes. Those methods are "
"listed in the left side of the dialog box. Begin by selecting the numbering "
"method you want by clicking once with the &LMB;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: footendnotes.docbook:101
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In the text box labeled <guilabel>Prefix text:</guilabel>, you can enter any "
"characters you want to appear <emphasis>before</emphasis> the footnote "
"number."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: footendnotes.docbook:103
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In the text box labeled <guilabel>Suffix text:</guilabel>, you can enter any "
"characters you want to appear <emphasis>after</emphasis> the footnote number."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: footendnotes.docbook:105
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can adjust the starting position of the footnote counter using the "
"spinbox labeled <guilabel>Start at:</guilabel>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: footendnotes.docbook:109
#, no-c-format
msgid "Change the appearance of separator line"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: footendnotes.docbook:110
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To change the appearance of the separator line, click on the tab labeled "
"<guilabel>Separator Line</guilabel>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: footendnotes.docbook:118
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can determine the alignment of the separator line by selecting "
"<guilabel>Left</guilabel>, <guilabel>Centered</guilabel> or <guilabel>Right</"
"guilabel>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: footendnotes.docbook:120
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Determine the length of the line using the spin box labeled <guilabel>Size "
"on page:</guilabel>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: footendnotes.docbook:121
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The spinbox labeled <guilabel>Width:</guilabel> is used to determine the "
"thickness of the seperator line."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: footendnotes.docbook:122
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Do not confuse this option with the <guilabel>Size on page:</guilabel> "
"option. The <guilabel>Width:</guilabel> is used to set the thickness of the "
"line, not its distance across the page."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: footendnotes.docbook:123
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Use the combo box labeled <guilabel>Style</guilabel> to determine what kind "
"of line is drawn."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: footendnotes.docbook:124
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Click <guibutton>OK</guibutton> to change the look of all footnotes or click "
"<guibutton>Cancel</guibutton> to keep the previous options."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: footendnotes.docbook:129
#, no-c-format
msgid "Change the placement of the footnotes"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: footendnotes.docbook:130
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can determine how much space separates the main text frame and the "
"footnotes. Select <menuchoice> <guimenu>Format</guimenu><guimenuitem>Page "
"Layout...</guimenuitem></menuchoice> from the menubar. This will bring up a "
"dialog:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: footendnotes.docbook:142
#, no-c-format
msgid "Click on the tab labeled <guilabel>Header &amp; Footer</guilabel>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: footendnotes.docbook:151
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"At the bottom of the dialog is a text box is labeled <guilabel>Spacing "
"between footnote and body</guilabel>. As the label suggests, you can use "
"this text box to specify the distance between the bottom edge of the main "
"frame, and the top edge of the footnotes. When you have entered the desired "
"spacing, click <guibutton>OK</guibutton>, and the footnotes will change "
"position on the page."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: footendnotes.docbook:159
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If both footnotes and endnotes are on the current page, the setting will "
"apply to the space between the body and the footnotes."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: footendnotes.docbook:165
#, no-c-format
msgid "Change the look of endnote entries"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: footendnotes.docbook:168
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To configure the appearance of endnotes, select <menuchoice> "
"<guimenu>Format</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Footnote...</guimenuitem></"
"menuchoice> from the menubar. A dialog will appear."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: footendnotes.docbook:177
#, no-c-format
msgid "Click on the tab labeled <guilabel>Endnotes</guilabel>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: footendnotes.docbook:188
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In the text box labeled <guilabel>Prefix text:</guilabel>, you can enter any "
"characters you want to appear <emphasis>before</emphasis> the endnote number."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: footendnotes.docbook:190
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In the text box labeled <guilabel>Suffix text:</guilabel>, you can enter any "
"characters you want to appear <emphasis>before</emphasis> the endnote number."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: footendnotes.docbook:192
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can adjust the starting position of the endnote counter using the "
"spinbox labeled <guilabel>Start at:</guilabel>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: footendnotes.docbook:194
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you want a line seperating the text of the document from your endnotes, "
"instructions for this can be found in the section entitled <link linkend="
"\"fn-config-line\">Change the appearance of separator line</link>."
msgstr ""

